1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:52,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気付くでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の天使 窓辺からやがて飛ぶたつ

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
ほとばしる熱いパッドスで 思い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
拡大なこう だけ食 opportunity

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
と思ったら

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:48,000
電流石を着るまで使った朝パラクターが 追いつから

12
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
たくさん置いて飲む池にも 判打にお飲み今日を

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
チョコココット湖で売り 終わり

14
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:05,740
さあなど あれに instal聚してやる

15
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:13,080
Oh, Commander Fuyutski. Good morning, sir.

16
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,460
Good morning, sir.

17
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:16,880
Good morning.

18
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:21,140
Well, you're up early today, sir.

19
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:24,260
I've got to represent Commander Akari uptown.

20
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:27,380
Ah, today's the city council meeting, isn't it?

21
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,240
An exercise in ennui.

22
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:33,300
Akari always sticks me with the most boring and tedious assignments.

23
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:35,920
I couldn't handle it without the Magi's help.

24
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:39,540
Speaking of which, election day is coming up, isn't it?

25
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:42,660
Yes, but the council really has no authority anyway.

26
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:45,320
Actually, the Magi run just about everything.

27
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,560
Really? You mean the same three supercomputers we use?

28
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:52,400
Yes. Our government is run by the majority decision of three different computers.

29
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,140
I suppose it's a sort of a form of democracy.

30
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,680
And the council members just go along with their decisions?

31
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:01,340
Well, it's been an effective form of government thus far.

32
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:03,260
This city really is built on science.

33
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,680
We're so lucky to be living in such a wonderful time.

34
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:07,300
Eh, technophiles.

35
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:11,060
You're running an experiment with Unit Zero this morning, aren't you?

36
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:16,420
Yes. We're going to be performing the second prolonged Ava activation test at 10.30.

37
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:17,880
Huh. I'll expect good news.

38
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:23,400
Abort the test! Break the circuits!

39
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,140
Cutting circuits.

40
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:30,260
Power supply restored.

41
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:34,620
It seems that one's the problem again.

42
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:39,240
Yes. It looks like the conversion efficiency is 0.8% lower than our calculation.

43
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:43,420
The conversion is barely within tolerance, though. What'll we do?

44
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,800
Let's try it again using the same configuration,

45
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:49,040
but lower the reciprocal conversion rate by 0.01.

46
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:51,700
All right. Let's start the experiment over again.

47
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:01,020
Hey! Hold the elevator!

48
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,020
Got it.

49
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,460
Man, it's been a while since I ran that hard.

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,040
So, what's with the black expression, Sunshine?

51
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,700
It's nausea from having to see you.

52
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,120
Yes. Hold one minute, please.

53
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,560
What?

54
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,560
Uh...

55
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,560
Uh...

56
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,560
Well...

57
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,560
Father...

58
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,500
Uh...

59
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:36,940
Well...

60
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,040
What is it? Hurry up!

61
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:40,880
Uh...

62
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,560
I'm supposed...

63
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,560
to tell my parents...

64
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:47,820
that an interview for

65
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:48,780
advanced

66
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,720
vocational education

67
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:54,520
is going to be

68
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:55,620
held at school.

69
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:58,200
I've delegated all of that to Katsuragi.

70
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,640
Don't bother me with such nonsense anymore.

71
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,000
Don't forward any more of these calls to me.

72
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:08,740
Huh?

73
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:08,940
Huh?

74
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:10,160
The power's out?

75
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:11,760
No, it can't be.

76
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:12,660
It's not possible.

77
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,120
Something's wrong.

78
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:16,280
An accident?

79
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,040
Perhaps Dr. Akagi made a mistake, huh?

80
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,940
The main power supply is shut down.

81
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,560
Voltage level is zero.

82
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:26,920
Uh...

83
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,220
It's not our fault.

84
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,920
Well, what do you think?

85
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:33,160
The backup supply should switch back on any second now.

86
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:33,940
No, sir.

87
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,580
The backup circuits aren't working either.

88
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:36,940
That can't be.

89
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,940
Which circuits are still functioning?

90
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:41,180
Only 1.2% of them.

91
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,180
Only 9 circuits from number 2567.

92
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,840
Connect all the remaining power circuits

93
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:48,740
to maintain the Magi and Central Dogma.

94
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:51,380
But that could interfere with our life support systems.

95
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,300
Do it!

96
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,600
We need the Magi!

97
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,640
Nozomu Takahashi wants to help you

98
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,060
form a more cheerful government.

99
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:00,720
Man, that Captain Katsuragi sure is lazy.

100
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:02,940
I mean, can't she at least make the time

101
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,560
to go and pick up her own laundry?

102
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:05,880
Hmm.

103
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:07,480
Huh?

104
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:12,000
Maybe Commander Akari was just really busy.

105
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,580
I don't think so.

106
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,100
And it wasn't like he hung up.

107
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:17,660
It sounded more like the line had failed.

108
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,680
Hey, are you a man or what?

109
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,780
Why do you let each and every little incident

110
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:22,700
get under your skin?

111
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:32,940
What are you doing?

112
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,700
Here, let me...

113
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:38,000
Hmm?

114
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,020
Huh?

115
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:39,700
Huh?

116
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:40,680
Huh?

117
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,560
Stupid thing!

118
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,320
It must be broken, damn it!

119
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:44,920
What?

120
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,680
Right here!

121
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:53,100
We'd better head for the command center.

122
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,440
If the backup power hasn't kicked in yet...

123
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,880
Then something's very wrong.

124
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,500
What's the backup system?

125
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,240
There are three backup circuits.

126
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:03,620
It's impossible for all of these to fail at once.

127
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:06,360
Then that means...

128
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,720
These circuit breakers didn't go on their own.

129
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,460
Someone did this intentionally.

130
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,340
Well, it would be a disaster

131
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:15,500
if an angel were to attack right now.

132
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:19,240
Radar's detected an unidentified object.

133
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,540
Projected landing point is in the form of Atami region.

134
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,440
It must be angel number eight.

135
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,740
Yeah, an angel.

136
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,000
What'll we do?

137
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:31,520
I guess the standard procedure is to go full alert status.

138
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:35,940
It looks like this one's heading straight for Tokyo 3 and NERV.

139
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:36,860
Looks like it.

140
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,460
Well, there's nothing we can do.

141
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:47,300
It's still advancing.

142
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,380
Any word yet from Tokyo 3?

143
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,420
They're still not responding to our transmissions.

144
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,800
What in the hell are those NERV guys doing?

145
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:57,380
I never thought I'd actually have to use one of these escape tubes.

146
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:01,080
I figured they were just holdovers that we held onto just for our peace of mind.

147
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,040
Well, being prepared is half the battle.

148
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:08,500
This one doesn't work either.

149
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,220
None of the facilities work.

150
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:11,180
This is odd.

151
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,380
Has something happened in the geo front?

152
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,700
A natural assumption.

153
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:18,120
Well, let's try to contact NERV headquarters.

154
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,000
The emergency phone isn't working either.

155
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,660
There's no answer on line 77.

156
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:25,620
None of them work.

157
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,760
No, it's disconnected.

158
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:30,180
This one, too.

159
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,400
The main and emergency cables are all down.

160
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,940
So what now?

161
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:43,240
What are you looking for?

162
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,880
What do you think, Doomkopf?

163
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,460
I'm looking for my emergency manual.

164
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:48,800
We should go to NERV headquarters ourselves.

165
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:49,800
That's right.

166
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:53,360
But before that, we're going to have to decide which of us will be this group's leader.

167
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:56,880
Naturally, I have the best qualifications.

168
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,400
Any objections?

169
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,520
Well, let's go.

170
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:03,360
Nervous over this way.

171
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,620
We can use the access port for Route 7.

172
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,440
But the doors don't work.

173
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,800
Oh, we can open it manually.

174
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,840
Well, there you go, Shinji.

175
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:13,940
This is your department.

176
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,260
You're the one who wants to be in charge.

177
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:20,640
But whenever going gets tough, you always defer to me.

178
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:26,000
That damn council always defers to us when the going gets tough.

179
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,800
Well, what did they say?

180
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:31,860
Those Tokyo 2 buttheads, they're getting ready to flee, of course.

181
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,480
The angel is still advancing.

182
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:40,220
In any case, we've got to try and make contact with NERV.

183
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,900
But how are we going to do that?

184
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,520
We fly there ourselves.

185
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:48,500
This is the 3rd District JASDF.

186
00:09:48,780 --> 00:09:51,280
An unidentified object is moving toward this area.

187
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:53,340
All residents must evacuate.

188
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,240
Oh, boy.

189
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,620
I got to report this to headquarters.

190
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:58,420
But how?

191
00:09:59,080 --> 00:09:59,980
Oh, man.

192
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,620
Hey, vote for Takahashi.

193
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:08,880
He's the candidate who remains calm, even in situations like this.

194
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,760
Oh, right.

195
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,520
I'm dying.

196
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,000
It's too hot in here.

197
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,860
The air conditioners are down, too.

198
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:19,840
If you're so hot, Katsuraki, why don't you take off your shirt?

199
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:22,960
There's no reason for you to be shy, you know.

200
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:27,400
Don't even think about trying to take advantage of this situation.

201
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,720
Yeah, right.

202
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:31,860
It's getting even warmer now that the air is getting stagnant.

203
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:36,000
It's hard to believe that this base has the world's most advanced technology.

204
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,620
Yeah, but look at the commanders.

205
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,420
Even in this heat, they're both still cool and in command.

206
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:48,360
It's hot.

207
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:49,640
Yes.

208
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:59,340
Emergency vehicle passing through.

209
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:01,800
Emergency vehicle passing through.

210
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,360
Hey, watch where you're driving.

211
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:05,180
Emergency vehicle passing through.

212
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,260
Oh, my God.

213
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:07,240
It's a dead end.

214
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:07,920
Stop.

215
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:09,060
It's okay.

216
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:09,920
Ram this sucker.

217
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:11,620
This is an emergency.

218
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,960
To hell with the barriers.

219
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:19,580
This geofront was designed to be a self-sufficient colony.

220
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:23,540
It's supposed to be able to operate even when completely isolated from the outside.

221
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:27,260
It's impossible for all the power sources to have broken down.

222
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:28,540
Someone caused this?

223
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,980
It would be a logical way to indirectly dissect this facility.

224
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:35,340
You mean that they could figure out Nerve's layout by the restoration process?

225
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:37,720
They are clever bastards.

226
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,100
I could run a dummy program through the Magi.

227
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:43,280
That would make it more difficult to get a complete grasp of our structure.

228
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:44,360
Make it so.

229
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,180
Yes, sir.

230
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:49,600
I can't believe that the first havoc wrecked upon our headquarters was caused by another

231
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,000
member of our own species.

232
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:54,460
Mankind's greatest enemy is man himself.

233
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,360
This usually only takes two minutes.

234
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:59,240
Are you sure this is the right way?

235
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,740
Of course I'm sure.

236
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:03,420
We'll be at the geofront any minute now.

237
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,980
Uh, haven't I heard that four times already?

238
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,780
Jeez, why do you have to nitpick everything?

239
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,560
You're always so negative.

240
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,160
Me?

241
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:11,580
What?

242
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,760
Silence, please.

243
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,380
Oh, what now, Wonder Girl?

244
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:15,480
Listen.

245
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,260
Tension all nerd personnel.

246
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,920
There is an angel approaching.

247
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,320
Tension all nerd personnel.

248
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,480
It's Yuga!

249
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:24,780
Hey, Yuga!

250
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:25,440
Hey!

251
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:27,000
Hey!

252
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:27,780
Hey!

253
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:29,480
There's an angel approaching.

254
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,520
An angel is approaching.

255
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:33,480
A new angel?

256
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,580
We can't waste any more time.

257
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:36,480
There's a shortcut.

258
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:39,060
Hey, don't forget that I'm the leader here.

259
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,000
So, where is this shortcut?

260
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:46,300
This way may be quick, but we look really stupid.

261
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,820
Hey, just what are the angels?

262
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,160
Huh?

263
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,760
Why are you asking now?

264
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,040
Well, I don't know.

265
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,680
It just doesn't make sense.

266
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,780
Angels are messengers from God, right?

267
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:59,220
Why are we fighting angels?

268
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,740
What, are you stupid?

269
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,660
They attacked us.

270
